1. Use-results survey (a survey conducted, in medical practice and using information collected from medical institutions, to detect or confirm the incidence by type of diseases etc. caused by adverse reactions to drugs and information on quality, efficacy and safety, being one of the following; the same applies below)
(a) General use-results survey (a survey conducted without setting conditions on the persons using the drug, excluding a comparative use-results survey under (c));
(b) Specified use-results survey (a survey conducted by setting conditions on the persons using the drug, such as children, the elderly, pregnant and parturient women, persons with renal or hepatic impairment and persons using the drug long term, excluding a comparative use-results survey under (c));
(c) Comparative use-results survey (a survey conducted by comparing information on persons using a specific drug with information on persons not using it).
